Change the delay metrics or r1 to avoid doing the load balancing.

@R1
----
int f1/0
delay 2000
end

VERIFY:
#sh int f1/0 -- check the delay 
#show ip eigrp topology
#sh ip route eigrp

These will:
R1 will add the new, higher delay to any route coming from 10.10.20.2 (L3S2).
The path through FastEthernet 1/0 will get a higher metric.
The routes via FastEthernet 0/0 (L3S1) will win, making it the single primary path in R1's routing table to match your active HSRP state.














